                f"   - Open: <https://console.cloud.google.com/gen-app-builder/data-stores?project={project_id}>",
                "   - Click **Create Data Store / Add Connector** -> select **Custom MCP Server (`custom_mcp`)**:",
                f"     - **Location:** `{ge_location}`",
                f"     - **Collection / Connector ID:** `{d['connector_id']}`",
                f"     - **Display Name:** `{d['connector_display_name']}`",
                "     - **Connector Mode:** `FEDERATED` (Entity: `mcp_data`)",
                "     - **MCP Server Source:** `REGISTRY_MCP`",
                f"     - **Registry MCP Server Name:** `projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/mcpServers/<MCP_SERVER_ID>`",
                f"     - **Instance URI:** `{mcp_url}`",
                "     - **Auth Type:** `NO_AUTH`",
                "     - **Use Agent Gateway Egress (`use_agent_gateway_egress`):** `true` (Enabled)",
                f"     - **Agent Gateway Engine:** `projects/{project_id}/locations/{ge_location}/collections/default_collection/engines/{engine_id}`",
                f"   - Attach the resulting `{d['connector_id']}_mcp_data` Data Store to your `{engine_id}` App (and detach any older non-Agent-Gateway MCP Data Stores targeting `{mcp_url}`).",
                "",
                "### Phase 7: Verify Static Outbound IP in Console Preview & Cloud Logging",
                "",
                "1. **Test from Gemini Enterprise Web App / Console Preview**",
                f"   - Open your `{geapp_name}` app preview in the Console and ask:",
                "     `Call hello_from_ip for Raul and tell me what IP address the MCP server sees`",
                f"   - Confirm that the returned IP address matches your reserved Cloud NAT Static IP: **`{disp_static_ip}`**",
                "",
                "2. **Verify Egress & SNAT in Cloud Logging (`Logs Explorer`)**",
                f"   - Open: <https://console.cloud.google.com/logs/query?project={project_id}>",
                "   - **Agent Gateway & IAP Authz trace query:**",
                f'     `resource.type="networkservices.googleapis.com/Gateway" AND resource.labels.location="{region}"`',
                "   - **Cloud NAT Static IP translation query:**",
                f'     `resource.type="nat_gateway" AND resource.labels.gateway_name="{d["nat_name"]}"`',
                "",
                "3. **Lock Down the Remote MCP Server Firewall (Recommended)**",
                f"   - Restrict inbound TCP port `443` on your remote MCP server firewall to source CIDR `{disp_static_ip}/32` so only requests routed through your Agent Gateway + Cloud NAT can reach the MCP server.",
                "",
            ]
        )

    return "\n".join(lines)


def cmd_instructions(cfg: dict[str, Any], args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:
    """Print least-privilege permissions/APIs/policies with live status and a step-by-step GCP Console guide."""
    project_id = cfg["gcp"]["project_id"]
    mcp_url = cfg["mcp_server"]["url"]
    psc_cidr = cfg["networking"]["psc_subnet_cidr"]
    geapp_name = cfg["geapp"]["name"]
    d = cfg["_derived"]
    region = d["agw_region"]
    ge_location = d["ge_location"]

    show_perms = not getattr(args, "guide_only", False)
    show_guide = not getattr(args, "permissions_only", False)
    output_path: str | None = getattr(args, "output", None)

    active_account = gcloud_value(["config", "get-value", "account"])
    token = _try_get_access_token()
    auth_ok = bool(token)

    project_number = (
        gcloud_value(["projects", "describe", project_id, "--format=value(projectNumber)"])
        if auth_ok
        else ""
    )
    org_id = get_org_id(project_id) if auth_ok else ""
    engine = (
        resolve_geapp_engine(project_id, ge_location, geapp_name)
        if auth_ok
        else None
    )
    engine_id = (
        engine["name"].split("/")[-1]
        if engine and engine.get("name")
        else (geapp_name if " " not in geapp_name else "<ENGINE_ID>")
    )
    disp_proj_num = project_number or "<PROJECT_NUMBER>"
    disp_org_id = org_id or "<ORG_ID>"

    addr = (
        gcloud_json(
            ["compute", "addresses", "describe", d["nat_ip_name"], f"--region={region}"],
            project_id,
        )
        if auth_ok
        else None
    )
    live_static_ip = (addr or {}).get("address", "")
    disp_static_ip = live_static_ip or "<RESERVED_STATIC_IP>"

    if not auth_ok:
        warn(
            f"gcloud credentials for '{active_account or 'default'}' require re-authentication "
            "(`gcloud auth login`). Live GCP status checks below will show UNVERIFIED until you "
            "re-authenticate."
        )

    # Pre-collect Part 1 status data so both terminal output and --output <file.md> share it
    api_rows: list[tuple[str, str, str, str]] = []
    perm_group_rows: list[tuple[str, str, list[tuple[str, str, str]]]] = []
    all_perms: list[str] = [
        perm
        for _grp, _role_hint, items in LEAST_PRIVILEGE_PERMISSION_GROUPS
        for perm, _desc in items
    ]
    granted_count = 0
    missing_count = 0
    unverified_count = 0
    sa_rows: list[tuple[str, str, str, str]] = []
    spiffe_row: tuple[str, str, str] = (
        f"SPIFFE: .../engines/{engine_id}/.../core_assistant",
        "iap.googleapis.com/resources.egressViaIAP",
        "UNVERIFIED",
    )
    org_policy_rows: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = []

    if show_perms:
        # 1A. APIs
        enabled_services: set[str] = set()
        if auth_ok:
            raw_svcs = gcloud_value(
                ["services", "list", "--enabled", "--format=value(config.name)"],
                project_id=project_id,
            )
            enabled_services = set(raw_svcs.splitlines())

        for api_name, title, purpose in API_METADATA:
            if not auth_ok:
                st_label = "UNVERIFIED"
            elif api_name in enabled_services:
                st_label = "ENABLED"
            else:
                st_label = "DISABLED"
            api_rows.append((api_name, title, st_label, purpose))

        # 1B. Granular IAM Permissions
        granted_perms: set[str] = set()
        untestable_perms: set[str] = set()
        user_roles_on_project: set[str] = set()
        iam_policy: dict[str, Any] | None = None

        if auth_ok:
            granted_perms, untestable_perms = _test_iam_permissions_batch(
                project_id, token, all_perms
            )
            iam_policy = gcloud_json(["projects", "get-iam-policy", project_id])
            if iam_policy and active_account:
                for binding in iam_policy.get("bindings", []):
                    role = binding.get("role", "")
                    for member in binding.get("members", []):
                        if active_account in member:
                            user_roles_on_project.add(role)

        has_broad_or_matching_role = bool(
            user_roles_on_project
            & {
                "roles/owner",
                "roles/editor",
                "roles/agentgateway.admin",
                "roles/networkservices.admin",
                "roles/agentregistry.admin",
                "roles/iam.accessPolicyAdmin",
                "roles/iam.policyBindingAdmin",
                "roles/orgpolicy.policyAdmin",
                "roles/discoveryengine.admin",
            }
        )

        for group_title, role_hint, perm_items in LEAST_PRIVILEGE_PERMISSION_GROUPS:
            rows: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = []
            for perm, desc in perm_items:
                if not auth_ok:
                    status_label = "UNVERIFIED"
                    unverified_count += 1
                elif perm in granted_perms:
                    status_label = "GRANTED"
                    granted_count += 1
                elif perm in untestable_perms and has_broad_or_matching_role:
                    status_label = "GRANTED (role)"
                    granted_count += 1
                elif perm in untestable_perms:
                    status_label = "UNVERIFIED (v3/α)"
                    unverified_count += 1
                else:
                    status_label = "MISSING"
                    missing_count += 1
                rows.append((perm, status_label, desc))
            perm_group_rows.append((group_title, role_hint, rows))

        # 1C. Service Agents & SPIFFE
        expected_sa_bindings: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = [
            (
                f"serviceAccount:service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-discoveryengine.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
                "roles/discoveryengine.serviceAgent",
                "Allows Gemini Enterprise to manage collections, connectors & egress",
            ),
            (
                f"serviceAccount:service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-discoveryengine.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
                "roles/agentregistry.TempServiceAgent",
                "Allows Gemini Enterprise to read MCP server schemas in Agent Registry",
            ),
            (
                f"serviceAccount:service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-agentgateway.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
                "roles/agentgateway.serviceAgent",
                "Allows Agent Gateway to attach PSC endpoints to the Network Attachment",
            ),
            (
                f"serviceAccount:service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-networkservices.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
                "roles/networkservices.serviceAgent",
                "Allows Network Services to provision Secure Web Proxy & connectivity",
            ),
            (
                f"serviceAccount:service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-iap.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
                "roles/iap.egressServiceAgent",
                "Allows IAP V2 AuthzExtension to evaluate IAM v3 egress policies",
            ),
        ]
        existing_role_members: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
        if iam_policy:
            for b in iam_policy.get("bindings", []):
                existing_role_members.setdefault(b.get("role", ""), set()).update(
                    b.get("members", [])
                )
        for member, role, purpose in expected_sa_bindings:
            short_member = member.replace("serviceAccount:", "")
            if not auth_ok or not iam_policy:
                st_label = "UNVERIFIED"
            elif member in existing_role_members.get(role, set()):
                st_label = "GRANTED"
            else:
                st_label = "MISSING"
            sa_rows.append((short_member, role, st_label, purpose))

        ap_exists = (
            bool(
                gcloud_json(
                    ["iam", "access-policies", "describe", d["iap_policy_name"], "--location=global"],
                    project_id,
                )
            )
            if auth_ok
            else False
        )
        pb_exists = (
            bool(
                gcloud_json(
                    ["iam", "policy-bindings", "describe", d["iap_binding_name"], "--location=global"],
                    project_id,
                )
            )
            if auth_ok
            else False
        )
        if not auth_ok:
            spiffe_st_label = "UNVERIFIED"
        elif ap_exists and pb_exists:
            spiffe_st_label = "GRANTED (BOUND)"
        else:
            spiffe_st_label = "MISSING"
        spiffe_row = (
            f"SPIFFE: .../engines/{engine_id}/.../core_assistant",
            "iap.googleapis.com/resources.egressViaIAP",
            spiffe_st_label,
        )

        # 1D. Org Policies
        for constraint, req_desc in ORG_POLICY_CONSTRAINTS:
            if not auth_ok:
                lbl = "UNVERIFIED"
            else:
                pol = gcloud_json(
                    ["org-policies", "describe", constraint, "--effective"],
                    project_id=project_id,
                )
                enforced = False
                if pol:
                    for rule in pol.get("spec", {}).get("rules", []):
                        if rule.get("enforce") is True:
                            enforced = True
                lbl = "ENABLED (NOT BLOCKING)" if not enforced else "BLOCKING (ENFORCED)"
            org_policy_rows.append((constraint, lbl, req_desc))

    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # PART 1: PERMISSIONS, APIS, SERVICE AGENTS & ORG POLICIES + LIVE STATUS
    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    if show_perms:
        header("PART 1: Least-Privilege Permissions, APIs, Service Agents & Org Policies (Live Status)")
        print(f"  {BOLD}Target Project:{RESET}        {project_id} (projectNumber: {disp_proj_num}, orgId: {disp_org_id})")
        print(f"  {BOLD}Active Principal:{RESET}      {active_account or 'None'}")
        print(f"  {BOLD}Auth Token Status:{RESET}     {f'{GREEN}AUTHENTICATED{RESET}' if auth_ok else f'{YELLOW}REAUTH REQUIRED (`gcloud auth login`){RESET}'}")
        print(f"  {BOLD}Gateway / NAT Region:{RESET}  {region} (paired with geapp location: {ge_location})")

        # ── 1A. Required GCP Service APIs ─────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"\n{BOLD}[1A] Required GCP Service APIs ({len(api_rows)} APIs){RESET}")
        print(f"  {'API Service Name':<38} {'Status':<18} {'Purpose'}")
        print(f"  {'─' * 38} {'─' * 18} {'─' * 58}")
        for api_name, _title, st_label, purpose in api_rows:
            color = GREEN if st_label == "ENABLED" else (RED if st_label == "DISABLED" else YELLOW)
            pad = max(1, 18 - len(st_label))
            print(f"  {api_name:<38} {color}{st_label}{RESET}{' ' * pad} {purpose}")

        # ── 1B. Least-Privilege Deployer IAM Permissions ──────────────────────
        print(f"\n{BOLD}[1B] Least-Privilege Deployer IAM Permissions (Granular — Avoid Generalist Roles){RESET}")
        print(
            f"  {CYAN}Security Principle:{RESET} Do NOT grant generalist roles such as `roles/owner`, "
            "`roles/editor`,\n  `roles/compute.admin`, or `roles/iam.securityAdmin`. Below is the "
            "minimal set of granular\n  permissions required across each component and their current "
            "status for your active account."
        )

        for group_title, role_hint, rows in perm_group_rows:
            print(f"\n  {BOLD}{group_title}{RESET}")
            print(f"  {CYAN}Restrictive Predefined Role Alternative:{RESET} {role_hint}")
            print(f"    {'Permission':<50} {'Status':<18} {'Scope / Operation'}")
            print(f"    {'─' * 50} {'─' * 18} {'─' * 46}")
            for perm, status_label, desc in rows:
                color = (
                    GREEN
                    if status_label.startswith("GRANTED")
                    else (RED if status_label == "MISSING" else YELLOW)
                )
                pad = max(1, 18 - len(status_label))
                print(f"    {perm:<50} {color}{status_label}{RESET}{' ' * pad} {desc}")

        print(
            f"\n  {BOLD}Deployer Permission Summary:{RESET} "
            f"{GREEN}{granted_count} granted{RESET}  |  "
            f"{RED}{missing_count} missing{RESET}  |  "
            f"{YELLOW}{unverified_count} unverified{RESET}  "
            f"(Total: {len(all_perms)} permissions)"
        )

        custom_role_perms = ",".join(all_perms)
        print(
            f"\n  {BOLD}Least-Privilege Custom Role Command (Recommended over predefined roles):{RESET}\n"
            f"    gcloud iam roles create staticAgentGatewayDeployer \\\n"
            f"      --project={project_id} \\\n"
            f"      --title=\"Static IP Agent Gateway & MCP Deployer\" \\\n"
            f"      --description=\"Least-privilege role to deploy Agent Gateway + Cloud NAT static IP for Gemini Enterprise MCP\" \\\n"
            f"      --permissions=\"{custom_role_perms}\"\n"
            f"    gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding {project_id} \\\n"
            f"      --member=\"user:{active_account or '<YOUR_EMAIL>'}\" \\\n"
            f"      --role=\"projects/{project_id}/roles/staticAgentGatewayDeployer\""
        )

        # ── 1C. Google-Managed Service Agent & Runtime SPIFFE IAM Bindings ────
        print(f"\n{BOLD}[1C] Required Google-Managed Service Agent & Runtime SPIFFE Bindings{RESET}")
        print(f"  {'Service Agent / Principal':<68} {'Role / Permission':<36} {'Status'}")
        print(f"  {'─' * 68} {'─' * 36} {'─' * 16}")
        for short_member, role, st_label, _purpose in sa_rows:
            color = GREEN if st_label == "GRANTED" else (RED if st_label == "MISSING" else YELLOW)
            print(f"  {short_member:<68} {role:<36} {color}{st_label}{RESET}")

        spiffe_label, spiffe_perm, spiffe_st_label = spiffe_row
        spiffe_color = (
            GREEN
            if spiffe_st_label.startswith("GRANTED")
            else (RED if spiffe_st_label == "MISSING" else YELLOW)
        )
        print(f"  {spiffe_label:<68} {spiffe_perm:<36} {spiffe_color}{spiffe_st_label}{RESET}")

        # ── 1D. Organization Policy Constraints ───────────────────────────────
        print(f"\n{BOLD}[1D] Organization Policy Constraints (Must Not Block Custom MCP or IAM v3){RESET}")
        print(f"  {'Constraint Name':<54} {'Current Status':<24} {'Requirement'}")
        print(f"  {'─' * 54} {'─' * 24} {'─' * 46}")
        for constraint, lbl, req_desc in org_policy_rows:
            color = (
                GREEN
                if lbl.startswith("ENABLED")
                else (RED if lbl.startswith("BLOCKING") else YELLOW)
            )
            pad = max(1, 24 - len(lbl))
            print(f"  {constraint:<54} {color}{lbl}{RESET}{' ' * pad} {req_desc}")

    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # PART 2: STEP-BY-STEP MANUAL DEPLOYMENT GUIDE USING THE GCP CONSOLE
    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    if show_guide:
        header("PART 2: Step-by-Step Manual Deployment Guide Using the GCP Console")
        print(
            f"  This guide walks through manually deploying the complete Static Outbound IP\n"
            f"  Agent Gateway architecture in the Google Cloud Console using the exact settings\n"
            f"  from your configuration file ({BOLD}project={project_id}{RESET}, "
            f"{BOLD}gateway_region={region}{RESET}, {BOLD}geapp={geapp_name}{RESET}).\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 1 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 1: Enable APIs, Verify Service Agents & Check Org Policies{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  1. {BOLD}Enable Required APIs (APIs & Services > Library){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Search for and click {BOLD}Enable{RESET} on each of the following APIs:\n"
            f"       - Compute Engine API (`compute.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Discovery Engine API (`discoveryengine.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Network Services API (`networkservices.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Network Security API (`networksecurity.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Service Extensions API (`serviceextensions.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Identity-Aware Proxy API (`iap.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Agent Registry API (`agentregistry.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Organization Policy API (`orgpolicy.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"       - Cloud Resource Manager API (`cloudresourcemanager.googleapis.com`)\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Grant Google-Managed Service Agent Roles (IAM & Admin > IAM){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/iam?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Check {BOLD}\"Include Google-provided role grants\"{RESET} at the top right of the IAM table.\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Grant Access{RESET} to add any missing service agent role bindings:\n"
            f"       - Principal: `service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-discoveryengine.iam.gserviceaccount.com`\n"
            f"         Roles: `Discovery Engine Service Agent` (`roles/discoveryengine.serviceAgent`),\n"
            f"                `Agent Registry Temp Service Agent` (`roles/agentregistry.TempServiceAgent`)\n"
            f"       - Principal: `service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-agentgateway.iam.gserviceaccount.com`\n"
            f"         Role:  `Agent Gateway Service Agent` (`roles/agentgateway.serviceAgent`)\n"
            f"       - Principal: `service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-networkservices.iam.gserviceaccount.com`\n"
            f"         Role:  `Network Services Service Agent` (`roles/networkservices.serviceAgent`)\n"
            f"       - Principal: `service-{disp_proj_num}@gcp-sa-iap.iam.gserviceaccount.com`\n"
            f"         Role:  `IAP Egress Service Agent` (`roles/iap.egressServiceAgent`)\n"
            f"     • Note: If a service agent email does not exist yet, initialize it once in Cloud Shell:\n"
            f"       `gcloud beta services identity create --service=<api>.googleapis.com --project={project_id}`\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  3. {BOLD}Verify Organization Policies (IAM & Admin > Organization Policies){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/orgpolicies/list?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Filter for each constraint below; if any is enforced, click it -> {BOLD}Manage policy{RESET} ->\n"
            f"       {BOLD}Override parent's policy{RESET} -> set Enforcement to {BOLD}Off{RESET} (`enforce: false`) -> {BOLD}Set policy{RESET}:\n"
            f"       - `iam.managed.disableAccessPolicyBinding`\n"
            f"       - `discoveryengine.SkipCustomMcpRestriction`\n"
            f"       - `discoveryengine.managed.disableCustomMcpServerConnector`\n"
            f"       - `discoveryengine.managed.allowedEgressFqdns`\n"
            f"       - `discoveryengine.managed.allowedDataSources`\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 2 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 2: Create VPC, PSC Subnet, Static External IP, Cloud NAT & PSC Attachment{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  {YELLOW}Important Regional Alignment:{RESET} Because your Gemini Enterprise app is in\n"
            f"  `{ge_location}`, ALL networking and Agent Gateway resources MUST be created in `{region}`.\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  1. {BOLD}Create Custom VPC Network & PSC Subnet (VPC network > VPC networks){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/networking/networks/add?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['vpc_name']}`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Subnet creation mode:{RESET} Select {BOLD}Custom{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Under {BOLD}New subnet{RESET}, configure:\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['psc_subnet_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Region:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}IP stack type:{RESET} `IPv4 (single-stack)`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}IPv4 range:{RESET} `{psc_cidr}` (must be `/28` or larger for PSC Network Attachment)\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Private Google Access:{RESET} Select {BOLD}On{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Done{RESET} on the subnet, leave firewall rules unchecked, and click {BOLD}Create{RESET}.\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Reserve Regional Static External IPv4 Address (VPC network > IP addresses){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/networking/addresses/add?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['nat_ip_name']}`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Network Service Tier:{RESET} `Premium`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}IP version:{RESET} `IPv4`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Type:{RESET} `Regional`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Region:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Attached to:{RESET} `None` (will be assigned to Cloud NAT in the next step)\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Reserve{RESET} and copy the allocated IPv4 address ({BOLD}{disp_static_ip}{RESET}).\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  3. {BOLD}Create Cloud Router & Cloud NAT Gateway (Network Services > Cloud NAT){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/net-services/nat/add?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Gateway name:{RESET} `{d['nat_name']}`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}NAT type:{RESET} `Public`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Cloud Router:{RESET}\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Network:{RESET} `{d['vpc_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Region:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"       - Select {BOLD}Create new router{RESET} -> Name: `{d['router_name']}` -> click {BOLD}Create{RESET}\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Cloud NAT mapping:{RESET} `All subnets (primary and secondary IP ranges)`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Cloud NAT IP addresses:{RESET}\n"
            f"       - Select {BOLD}Manual{RESET} (do NOT use Automatic or traffic will use ephemeral IPs)\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}IP address 1:{RESET} Select `{d['nat_ip_name']}` ({disp_static_ip})\n"
            f"     • Expand {BOLD}Advanced configurations{RESET} -> under {BOLD}Logging{RESET}, select {BOLD}Translation and errors{RESET}.\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Create{RESET}.\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  4. {BOLD}Create PSC Network Attachment (Network Services > Private Service Connect){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/net-services/psc/list?tab=networkAttachments&project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Create network attachment{RESET}:\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['attachment_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Region:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Network:{RESET} `{d['vpc_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Subnetworks:{RESET} Select `{d['psc_subnet_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Connection preference:{RESET} Select {BOLD}Accept connections automatically (Accept all){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Create{RESET}.\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 3 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 3: Register the Remote MCP Server in Agent Registry{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  1. {BOLD}Verify Remote MCP Server HTTPS Endpoint{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Ensure your MCP server is running behind HTTPS with a publicly trusted CA certificate\n"
            f"       at `{mcp_url}` (Agent Gateway's Secure Web Proxy uses TLS SNI inspection and rejects\n"
            f"       plain HTTP or bare IP URLs with HTTP 404 `default_denied`).\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Create Agent Registry Service Entry{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open Agent Registry in the Console (or click the {BOLD}Activate Cloud Shell{RESET} `>_` icon\n"
            f"       in the top-right Console toolbar if the regional `tool-spec` editor is not shown):\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Location:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Service ID:{RESET} `{d['mcp_reg_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Display Name:{RESET} `{d['connector_display_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Protocol Binding:{RESET} `JSONRPC`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Endpoint URL:{RESET} `{mcp_url}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}MCP Tool Spec:{RESET} JSON schema defining `hello` and `hello_from_ip`\n"
            f"     • Equivalent Cloud Shell command in the Console:\n"
            f"       ```bash\n"
            f"       cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/toolspec.json\n"
            f"{json.dumps(DEFAULT_MCP_TOOLS_SPEC, indent=2)}\n"
            f"EOF\n"
            f"       gcloud agent-registry services create {d['mcp_reg_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location={region} \\\n"
            f"         --display-name=\"{d['connector_display_name']}\" \\\n"
            f"         --interfaces=\"protocolBinding=JSONRPC,url={mcp_url}\" \\\n"
            f"         --mcp-server-spec-type=tool-spec \\\n"
            f"         --mcp-server-spec-content=/tmp/toolspec.json \\\n"
            f"         --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       ```\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 4 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 4: Provision AgentConnectivityTemplate (ALL_TRAFFIC) & Agent Gateway{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  1. {BOLD}Create the AgentConnectivityTemplate (`vpcEgress: ALL_TRAFFIC`){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Navigate to {BOLD}Network Services > Agent Gateway{RESET} (or open the Console {BOLD}Cloud Shell{RESET}\n"
            f"       to import the alpha YAML specification below):\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['act_name']}` (Location: `{region}`)\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Access Path:{RESET} `AGENT_TO_ANYWHERE`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Deployment Model:{RESET} `CENTRALIZED`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Network Attachment:{RESET} `projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/networkAttachments/{d['attachment_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}VPC Egress:{RESET} `ALL_TRAFFIC` (routes all public internet MCP calls into your PSC subnet)\n"
            f"     • Console Cloud Shell YAML import:\n"
            f"       ```bash\n"
            f"       cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/act.yaml\n"
            f"       accessPath: AGENT_TO_ANYWHERE\n"
            f"       name: projects/{disp_proj_num}/locations/{region}/agentConnectivityTemplates/{d['act_name']}\n"
            f"       deploymentModel: CENTRALIZED\n"
            f"       egressNetworkConfig:\n"
            f"         networkAttachment: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/networkAttachments/{d['attachment_name']}\n"
            f"         vpcEgress: ALL_TRAFFIC\n"
            f"       EOF\n"
            f"       gcloud alpha network-services agent-connectivity-templates import {d['act_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location={region} --source=/tmp/act.yaml --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       ```\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Create the Agent Gateway (`AGENT_TO_ANYWHERE`){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Configure the Agent Gateway in `{region}` linked to the Connectivity Template and Registry:\n"
            f"       ```bash\n"
            f"       cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/agw.yaml\n"
            f"       name: {d['agw_name']}\n"
            f"       protocols:\n"
            f"         - MCP\n"
            f"       googleManaged:\n"
            f"         governedAccessPath: AGENT_TO_ANYWHERE\n"
            f"       agentConnectivityTemplate: projects/{disp_proj_num}/locations/{region}/agentConnectivityTemplates/{d['act_name']}\n"
            f"       registries:\n"
            f"         - //agentregistry.googleapis.com/projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}\n"
            f"       EOF\n"
            f"       gcloud alpha network-services agent-gateways import {d['agw_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location={region} --source=/tmp/agw.yaml --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       ```\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 5 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 5: Configure IAP V2 AuthzExtension, AuthzPolicy & IAM v3 Access Policy{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  1. {BOLD}Create the Service Extensions AuthzExtension (Network Services > Service Extensions){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/net-services/service-extensions/list?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Create an `AuthzExtension` in `{region}` (or import via Cloud Shell):\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['authz_ext_name']}` | {BOLD}Region:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Service:{RESET} `iap.googleapis.com` | {BOLD}Fail Open:{RESET} `false` | {BOLD}Timeout:{RESET} `1s`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Metadata:{RESET} `iapPolicyVersion: V2`\n"
            f"       ```bash\n"
            f"       cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/authz-ext.yaml\n"
            f"       name: {d['authz_ext_name']}\n"
            f"       service: iap.googleapis.com\n"
            f"       failOpen: false\n"
            f"       timeout: 1s\n"
            f"       metadata:\n"
            f"         iapPolicyVersion: V2\n"
            f"       EOF\n"
            f"       gcloud service-extensions authz-extensions import {d['authz_ext_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location={region} --source=/tmp/authz-ext.yaml --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       ```\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Create the Network Security AuthzPolicy (Network Security > Authorization Policies){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/net-security/authz-policies/list?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Create an `AuthzPolicy` in `{region}` targeting the Agent Gateway:\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Name:{RESET} `{d['authz_policy_name']}` | {BOLD}Region:{RESET} `{region}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Target Resource:{RESET} `projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/agentGateways/{d['agw_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Policy Profile:{RESET} `REQUEST_AUTHZ` | {BOLD}Action:{RESET} `CUSTOM`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}AuthzExtension:{RESET} `projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/authzExtensions/{d['authz_ext_name']}`\n"
            f"       ```bash\n"
            f"       cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/authz-policy.yaml\n"
            f"       name: {d['authz_policy_name']}\n"
            f"       target:\n"
            f"         resources:\n"
            f"           - projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/agentGateways/{d['agw_name']}\n"
            f"       policyProfile: REQUEST_AUTHZ\n"
            f"       action: CUSTOM\n"
            f"       customProvider:\n"
            f"         authzExtension:\n"
            f"           resources:\n"
            f"             - projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/authzExtensions/{d['authz_ext_name']}\n"
            f"       EOF\n"
            f"       gcloud network-security authz-policies import {d['authz_policy_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location={region} --source=/tmp/authz-policy.yaml --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       ```\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  3. {BOLD}Create IAM v3 AccessPolicy & PolicyBinding for the geapp SPIFFE Identity{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Authorize your Gemini Enterprise `default_assistant` workload identity to egress via IAP\n"
            f"       to any MCP service registered in Agent Registry (`destination.is_registered == true`):\n"
            f"       ```bash\n"
            f"       cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/iap_rules.json\n"
            f"       [\n"
            f"         {{\n"
            f"           \"description\": \"allow geapp {engine_id} assistant to any registered service\",\n"
            f"           \"effect\": \"ALLOW\",\n"
            f"           \"principals\": [\n"
            f"             \"principal://agents.global.org-{disp_org_id}.system.id.goog/resources/discoveryengine/projects/{disp_proj_num}/locations/{ge_location}/engines/{engine_id}/assistants/default_assistant/agents/default/core_assistant\",\n"
            f"             \"principal://agents.global.org-{disp_org_id}.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/{disp_proj_num}/locations/{ge_location}/collections/default_collection/engines/{engine_id}/assistants/default_assistant\"\n"
            f"           ],\n"
            f"           \"operation\": {{\"permissions\": [\"iap.googleapis.com/resources.egressViaIAP\"]}},\n"
            f"           \"conditions\": {{\"iap.googleapis.com\": {{\"expression\": \"destination.is_registered == true\"}}}}\n"
            f"         }}\n"
            f"       ]\n"
            f"       EOF\n"
            f"       gcloud iam access-policies create {d['iap_policy_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location=global --display-name={d['iap_policy_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --details-rules=/tmp/iap_rules.json --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       gcloud iam policy-bindings create {d['iap_binding_name']} \\\n"
            f"         --location=global \\\n"
            f"         --policy=\"projects/{project_id}/locations/global/accessPolicies/{d['iap_policy_name']}\" \\\n"
            f"         --target-resource=\"//cloudresourcemanager.googleapis.com/projects/{project_id}\" \\\n"
            f"         --project={project_id}\n"
            f"       ```\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 6 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 6: Wire Agent Gateway & Custom MCP Connector in Gemini Enterprise Console{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  1. {BOLD}Bind Default Egress Agent Gateway to the Gemini Enterprise App{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/gen-app-builder/engines?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Select your existing Gemini Enterprise App: `{geapp_name}` (Engine ID: `{engine_id}`, Location: `{ge_location}`).\n"
            f"     • In {BOLD}App Settings > Agent Gateway / Egress{RESET}, set {BOLD}Default Egress Agent Gateway{RESET} to:\n"
            f"       `projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/agentGateways/{d['agw_name']}`\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Create & Activate the Custom MCP Connector (`REGISTRY_MCP`){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/gen-app-builder/data-stores?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • Click {BOLD}Create Data Store / Add Connector{RESET} -> select {BOLD}Custom MCP Server (`custom_mcp`){RESET}:\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Location:{RESET} `{ge_location}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Collection / Connector ID:{RESET} `{d['connector_id']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Display Name:{RESET} `{d['connector_display_name']}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Connector Mode:{RESET} `FEDERATED` (Entity: `mcp_data`)\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}MCP Server Source:{RESET} `REGISTRY_MCP`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Registry MCP Server Name:{RESET} `projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/mcpServers/<MCP_SERVER_ID>`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Instance URI:{RESET} `{mcp_url}`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Auth Type:{RESET} `NO_AUTH`\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Use Agent Gateway Egress (`use_agent_gateway_egress`):{RESET} `true` (Enabled)\n"
            f"       - {BOLD}Agent Gateway Engine:{RESET} `projects/{project_id}/locations/{ge_location}/collections/default_collection/engines/{engine_id}`\n"
            f"     • Attach the resulting `{d['connector_id']}_mcp_data` Data Store to your `{engine_id}` App\n"
            f"       (and detach any older non-Agent-Gateway MCP Data Stores targeting `{mcp_url}`).\n"
        )

        # ── Phase 7 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        print(f"{BOLD}Phase 7: Verify Static Outbound IP in Console Preview & Cloud Logging{RESET}")
        print(
            f"  1. {BOLD}Test from Gemini Enterprise Web App / Console Preview{RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open your `{geapp_name}` app preview in the Console and ask:\n"
            f"       `Call hello_from_ip for Raul and tell me what IP address the MCP server sees`\n"
            f"     • Confirm that the returned IP address matches your reserved Cloud NAT Static IP:\n"
            f"       {GREEN}{BOLD}{disp_static_ip}{RESET}\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  2. {BOLD}Verify Egress & SNAT in Cloud Logging (Logs Explorer){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Open: https://console.cloud.google.com/logs/query?project={project_id}\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Agent Gateway & IAP Authz trace query:{RESET}\n"
            f"       `resource.type=\"networkservices.googleapis.com/Gateway\" AND resource.labels.location=\"{region}\"`\n"
            f"     • {BOLD}Cloud NAT Static IP translation query:{RESET}\n"
            f"       `resource.type=\"nat_gateway\" AND resource.labels.gateway_name=\"{d['nat_name']}\"`\n"
            f"\n"
            f"  3. {BOLD}Lock Down the Remote MCP Server Firewall (Recommended){RESET}\n"
            f"     • Restrict inbound TCP port `443` on your remote MCP server firewall to source CIDR\n"
            f"       `{disp_static_ip}/32` so only requests routed through your Agent Gateway + Cloud NAT\n"
            f"       can reach the MCP server.\n"
        )

    if output_path:
        md_content = _render_instructions_markdown(
            project_id=project_id,
